<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Heraklion</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Chandax, Candia, Iraklio, Herakleion, Iraklion</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Heraklion is the largest city and capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crete">Crete</a>. It was founded in the 820s as Chandax, the fortified capital of the Andalusi Arab <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">emirate</a> that ruled the island until the Byzantine general Nikephoros Phokas took it in 961. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venice">Venice</a> it was called Candia and withstood an Ottoman siege from 1648 to 1669, one of the longest in history. The Minoan palace of Knossos lies nearby.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/heraklion.jpg" alt="Heraklion" width="320" height="389" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: SilentResident (compilation, sources to attribute see above; if any of the sources used in the Montage are removed fr... · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Heraklion_Montage_L.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
